				// Same fade curves, moved in time: leaving shapes 0.15 s earlier, appearing ones 0.05 s later, so a
				// leaving shape has faded out before a new shape appears over it. Shapes at the bottom (no box
				// around them stays) keep the unshifted fade: what arrives covers them in a cross-fade.
				const qo = (shift) => EM(clamp((tau - 0.15 - pr.delay - shift) / 0.9));
